h backoff, then the criterion is left incomplete (no .eval.yaml, no ledger row) and the run continues to the next criterion.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A transient model/transport error is RETRYABLE (3 attempts, exp backoff 1s/2s/4s), then the criterion is left incomplete (no ledger row; run continues).'","No AC exercises retry exhaustion or asserts the run continues with the criterion left un-admitted and no ledger row."],"finding":"The described transient-error retry behavior (3 attempts, exp backoff, then 'the criterion is left incomplete (no ledger row; run continues)') has no covering acceptance criterion; every other disposition branch (reproduce, drift, budget-exceed, cap-breach, resume, shadow-skip) has one, but the retry/incomplete path is unverified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f72901435286fe777","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Failure disposition; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n2b60cde72952d220","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A finder call keeps failing transiently; the runner must retry 3x then move on without an orphan spec or ledger row."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[non-codebase] A live admission run has completed over the full candidate set wi' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (principal is missing or a placeholder value; privilege_posture is missing or a placeholder value; instrument is missing or a placeholder value; justification is missing or a placeholder value); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] Each drift-report entry has a ticket linked `discovered_from` the' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (privilege_posture is missing or a placeholder value; instrument is missing or a placeholder value; justification is missing or a placeholder value); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["prerequisite-consistency"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3947,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Subject: The estimate tier follows the criterion's exec routing (criteria.effective_routing, ADR 0033)","Prerequisite: adds \"criteria-eval-cheap\": 0.03 and \"criteria-eval-agent\": 0.25 ... raises ValueError on any other tier"],"finding":"The subject plan pre-flights `ledger.reserve(estimate_usd, ledger_path=<epic ledger>, cap_usd=250.0, reserve_usd=0.0)` and states reserve_usd=0 yields a ceiling of exactly $250. The ledger prerequisite parameterizes `reserve()` with keyword-only `cap_usd` and `reserve_usd`, which supports the subject's $250/$0 call. However, the subject asserts the estimate tier follows `criteria.effective_routing` (ADR 0033) with tiers driving the estimate, while the ledger prerequisite adds only the estimate keys `criteria-eval-cheap` (0.03) and `criteria-eval-agent` (0.25) and raises ValueError on any unregistered tier. The subject never states which of these two keys its routing maps to, nor confirms `effective_routing` yields exactly those two tier names. If the subject's routing produces tier names other than `criteria-eval-cheap`/`criteria-eval-agent`, `estimate()` would raise ValueError. This is an unresolved mapping gap between the routing model in the subject and the fixed estimate keys the prerequisite provides.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f699bb5f4dad98218","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Budget enforcement","norm_id":"n20815773a6dee651","priority":0.2053,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State explicitly that effective_routing maps DET-excluded criteria to the two registered estimate keys criteria-eval-cheap and criteria-eval-agent.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["prerequisite-consistency"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Emitter: input is a deterministic, model-free provenance descriptor rendered from the row's stable fields ... NOT resolved from any store","Subject: rebuilds dataset + gold_set (1:1 input/label) from only the reproducing cases, each case's input being the runnable rehydrated material"],"finding":"The emitter prerequisite emits case `input` as a model-free provenance descriptor derived from the row's stable fields (criterion, direction, tier, sorted signals, norm_id/review_event_uuid, rank), which is explicitly NOT resolved from any store. The subject plan states it reuses the emitter's skeleton UNCHANGED but rebuilds `dataset` + `gold_set` from reproducing cases with each case's `input` being the runnable rehydrated material (the sidecar row's description/children). This is consistent — the runner replaces the descriptor input with rehydrated material. However, the emitter derives the case `id` as `<prompt_id>-<direction>-<rank>` and the gold_set as one `{input, label}` per case with `input` matching the case's `input`. Since the subject runner rebuilds `dataset` + `gold_set` (1:1) from reproducing cases with new `input`, but reuses the emitter's `gold_set` field only within the rebuild, the 1:1 input/label correspondence must be preserved. This is consistent. No genuine incompatibility on identifiers or field derivation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4ff699a1ed1d2416","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Disposition","norm_id":"n9e99076539ebcbb5","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"na","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"956a1e0df3201633","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["f276c25d69ca932d",7957],"description_boxes":["e91772ccb5e6ce5f",0],"file_impact":["b6f57b21b6f013db",5],"ticket_id":["9322f7dbb87ae5ac",19